# Project Context

- Java 21 Maven project.
- Use the checked-in Maven Wrapper (`./mvnw`), never depend on a global `mvn`.
- On this Mac, Java 21 is Corretto at
  `$HOME/Library/Java/JavaVirtualMachines/corretto-21.0.12/Contents/Home`.
- If Java is not discovered, run:
  `JAVA_HOME="$HOME/Library/Java/JavaVirtualMachines/corretto-21.0.12/Contents/Home" ./mvnw test`.
- Production code: `src/main/java/com/practice`.
- Tests: `src/test/java/com/practice`, using JUnit Jupiter.
- Run targeted tests while iterating:
  `./mvnw -Dtest=ClassNameTest test`.
- Run `./mvnw test` before completing substantive Java changes.
- Match the package of tests to the production class package.
- Do not commit `target/`, IDE metadata, or generated class files.
- Branch/commit naming: see `git-branch-commit.mdc`
  (`{package}/{problem-kebab-case}`, topic-prefixed commit messages).
